\subsection{Traffic Congestion Dataset}
Highly dynamic and congested traffic environments are ubiquitous in the real world, but few data sets emphasize these scenarios.
To address this challenge, we use the Carla simulator\cite{dosovitskiy2017carla} to simulate dynamic and crowded scenes, and generate the \textbf{Traffic Congestion Dataset (TCD)}. 
We collected several sequences from four maps and the sensors on the vehicle include stereo cameras and 64-channel LiDAR data.
In addition to the ego vehicle, hundreds of other dynamic or static vehicles are on the map to simulate dynamic and crowded environments in reality.
In each segment sequence of the Waymo Open Dataset\cite{sun2020scalability}, the average number of vehicles is less than one hundred, while in our Traffic Congestion dataset, the number of vehicles per segment sequence ranges from 200 to 300.
The dense and dynamic flow of vehicles pose challenges to accurate self-localization and MOT.


